<Page title="About Grand Tour" kicker="About this site" description="What Grand Tour is, who publishes it, and how its France travel stories are written, sourced and kept up to date." lede="Grand Tour is a travel blog for people planning a trip to France beyond the obvious: the regions, the food and wine, the walking and cycling, and the slower ways of getting around.">
  <h2>Who publishes it</h2>
  <p><strong>Grand Tour is published by Tourground.</strong> Tourground runs a directory of verified local travel companies around the world, and some travel brands in its network, including the French road-trip specialist Rond-Point, are connected to Tourground. Our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a> sets out the relationship in full.</p>
  <h2>What we write</h2>
  <p>Story-led, practical posts about France: where to go, how a region feels, what is worth your time, and how to put a trip together. We want you to finish a story knowing both why you would go and how you would actually do it.</p>
  <p>Every story ends with a “Plan this trip” box pointing you to a local operator through the Tourground directory, so that you can talk to a company on the ground if you would rather not plan everything yourself.</p>
  <h2>How we write</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sourced.</strong> Practical facts, such as opening seasons, booking rules, transport and the law, link to the official source in the text, and every story lists its sources at the end.</li>
    <li><strong>Dated.</strong> Every story shows when it was published and when its practical details were last checked. Timetables, rules and opening dates change, so check the sources before you book.</li>
    <li><strong>Nothing invented.</strong> We do not publish made-up reviews, quotes, testimonials, prices or statistics. If we cannot source something, we leave it out.</li>
    <li><strong>Honest pictures.</strong> Our photographs are real, freely licensed photographs from Wikimedia Commons, credited to their authors. See <a href="/photo-credits/">photo credits</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Labelled advertising.</strong> If we ever publish paid content, it will be labelled “Advertisement feature”.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <p>We do not sell trips, take bookings or handle payments. Any booking you make is with the company you choose.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>If something on this site is wrong or out of date, please tell us by email with the page address and, if you can, a source. We will check it, correct the story if needed and update its date.</p>
</Page>
